<title>TURKEY: Turkish Tupras losses surge in 1996.</title>
<headline>Turkish Tupras losses surge in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share loss (lira)     4,060.80  vs   1,069.70</p>
<p>    Loss			   18,972.05  vs   4,997.64</p>
<p>    Net sales		   343,512.18  vs 162,300.78</p>
<p>    Operating loss	     32,202.52  vs   6,222.48</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	 14,913.21  vs   3,072.08</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		 1,284.42  vs   1,609.74</p>
<p>    Total debts		 141,976.26  vs  57,770.03</p>
<p>    Equity			 10,367.18  vs  15,790.91</p>
<p>    Capital			 4,672.00  vs   4,672.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Largely state owned oil refiner Tupras - Turkiye Petrol Rafinerileri A.S. is slated for privatisation with 96.41 percent of its capital owned by Turkey's privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875 GUZ EKS</p>
</text>
